    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37176" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pŏsĭtīvus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>positive</i>, in gram. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Settled by arbitrary appointment</i> or <i>agreement</i> (opp. to natural): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nomina non positiva esse sed naturalia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					10, 4</span></i>
			
			<i>in lemm.</i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Positivum nomen. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>An adjective in the positive degree</i>, Cledon. p.
			1893 P.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>A substantive</i>, <i><span class="en">Macr. S.
				1, 4, 9</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
